chunk 1: 15 units, 28 patches applied (28 changes logged), 3 issues without patch, 0 patches failed
  MANUAL unit 6 [minor] text_flags / a̭śī̱yā'': The flag treats the marks as stray and suggests 'aśīya', but the Devanagari reads 'अशीयाऽऽ विवासेयं': the long ā and avagraha-type signs record the contraction aśīya + ā (the next word begins ā-vivāseyam or the ā is a separate particle). Deleting them would drop a printed vowel, and the split/translation do not account for any ā.
         suggested fix: Keep the flag as 'unusual contraction aśīyā-ऽ, probably aśīya ā; sense of ā unclear', not a plain deletion; mention in notes that ā is untranslated.
  MANUAL unit 6 [minor] english / Like one in the heat reaching shade, free from fault may I attain it: The English (and Hindi) supply 'one in', 'reaching' and an object 'it'; the line has only ghṛṇiḥ iva chāyām (heat ... shade) arapāḥ aśīya. The notes claim 'only what the grammar needs' is supplied, which is not so.
         suggested fix: Keep to the text: 'Like heat (seeking) shade, free from fault may I attain' is still a supply; move 'one in', 'reaching' and 'it' to the notes and leave the object of aśīya open.
  MANUAL unit 12 [error] english / as even a boy bows towards his father: kumāraḥ cit is third person and cannot be subject of the 1 sg. nānāma; the draft uses nānāma twice ('I have bowed' and 'a boy bows'), and 'as' (जैसे) is admittedly not in the text. The comparison is invented.
         suggested fix: Do not split the verb: render e.g. 'I, even a boy, have bowed towards the father who is greeted / as he approaches, O Rudra' or mark the line as unresolved; remove the supplied 'as ... as'. Hindi 'जैसे बालक भी ... झुकता है' needs the same repair.
